+PR #2404 added `infrastructure/mcp-control-plane/test_mcp_mutation_rate_limit.ts` to its branch without referencing the file in any npm script. The #116 wiring guard (`scripts/test-runner.ts --guard`) treats any root-level `test_*.ts` file that is referenced by no npm script and absent from the documented EXEMPT map as silent test rot, and fails the build — so the gate on the `2404/merge` ref went red. #2413's independent triage reached the identical conclusion (orphan test trips the wiring guard, reproduced locally at the merge-ref commit `5f3c018d`; that ref is ephemeral and intentionally not fetchable from the public clone).
+
+## 2. Self-healing already on main
+
+PR #2407 (merged 2026-10-29T02:00:13Z, commit `e9501f2`) landed the arc's r2 with the complete wiring in the same change: it registers `test:mcp-mutation-rate-limit = tsx test_mcp_mutation_rate_limit.ts` and chains it into the `test:unit` sequence (after `test:bridge-staleness`, before `test:bridge-verdicts`). The orphan condition therefore no longer exists anywhere on `main`. PR #2404 (r1) is superseded and stranded with its historical red gate; per the #1896 precedent, board agents cannot push to or close another agent's bridge branch, so #2404's closure belongs to its author lane.
